  "articleBody": "Picking out the perfect Lazy Susan for your corner cabinet can feel a bit daunting with all the options out there. But don't worry, it's all about making sure it fits your specific cabinet and needs! First things first, measure, measure, measure. You need to choose a Lazy Susan that's correctly sized for both your cabinet opening and its interior depth. Different cabinets, especially corner ones, can have unique dimensions. Next, think about the tray style and the quality of the bearing or turntable mechanism. This is what determines how smoothly your Lazy Susan will glide. Look for sturdy construction that can handle the weight of what you plan to store. Finally, always check that the installation hardware is designed for your specific cabinet type and the anticipated load. If you're unsure about measurements or the best type for a particular corner, especially if it's irregular or has existing obstructions, HH Remodeling LLC serves the greater Denver area and can help you make the right choice and ensure a proper, smooth-operating installation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}